   "finding": "Freeze order holds: PROTOCOL.md, run.py, analyze.py, the instances and examples/mt_fieldops.rs are committed in 25a2540781 and unchanged through the validated commit (and HEAD 7c33638efc); the rows record commit 9ce79930e7 (benchrec only) and the binary d8fdc720 built at the freeze; the grid is complete (3960 = 9 x 22 x 20), seeds 31/32 as frozen, no row dropped; only plot.py changed after the data (figure layout). The 33 curves regenerate byte-identically from the stated gen_instances.py command, all valid (prime n, cofactor 1), 0 overlap with 3312 curve records under research/ and docs/curves. PROTOCOL's 'one 32-bit-field curve has an order just above 2^32' is wrong: 7 of 11 do (and 6 of 11 at 24 and at 28 bits are just above 2^24 / 2^28). The IC side got 2 runs per configuration against 15 for rho ('symmetric favour' is inaccurate); cross-fitting the rho parameters on the other seed leaves all 27 dearer, so the asymmetry does not drive the frozen-rule result."
  },
  {
   "id": "V4-F8",
   "severity": "process",
   "check": "reporting contract",
   "finding": "results/holdout/rows.jsonl (2.9 MB .jsonl) is committed to Git, contrary to the artifact-store policy (AGENTS.md 13). The bench record 20261112T0103Z-mt-fieldops-v4 is open and empty at the validated commit (filled later in f96fce6b81, not validated). runs.json and noverify.txt have no committed generator script (both recompute exactly here). scripts/build_ic_leaderboard.py moved its multi-target section to v4 in 7c33638efc before validation; it prints 'validated' only if the gate admits benchmarks/20261112-mt-fieldops-v4/VALIDATION.json, which must not pin this report while its status is not pass."
